---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="For Partners | Hitori Jigyo Lab"
  description="English media overview for SaaS affiliate managers and partner teams reviewing Hitori Jigyo Lab."
>
  <section class="page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">For Partners</p>
    <h1>Hitori Jigyo Lab Media Overview</h1>
    <p>
      Hitori Jigyo Lab is a Japanese-language content site for solo founders, freelancers,
      and small business owners who want to use AI, SaaS, websites, newsletters, CRM,
      analytics, and online business tools in a practical way.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="text-page partner-page">
    <div class="trust-summary">
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">Site</p>
        <h2>Hitori Jigyo Lab</h2>
        <p>Japanese-language editorial site operated by TATSU.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">Audience</p>
        <h2>Japan-based solo operators</h2>
        <p>Freelancers, sole proprietors, small business owners, and side-project builders.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">Format</p>
        <h2>Editorial content</h2>
        <p>Hands-on reviews, setup notes, comparison guides, and transparent affiliate disclosures.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h2>What We Publish</h2>
    <p>We publish practical Japanese articles about overseas SaaS tools, AI workflows, website building, newsletters, CRM, ecommerce, analytics, and affiliate program research. The site is built as an ongoing solo-business lab, so application logs, rejected applications, profile improvements, and decision records are also documented.</p>
    <p>Our goal is not to push generic deals or coupon traffic. We focus on helping Japanese readers understand whether a tool fits a small operation before they sign up.</p>

    <h2>Primary Reader Intent</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Choosing a website, newsletter, CRM, analytics, or ecommerce tool</li>
      <li>Understanding pricing, free plans, cancellation flow, and Japanese-language usability</li>
      <li>Learning how overseas SaaS can be used in a small Japanese business</li>
      <li>Comparing tools before making a low-risk first trial</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Promotion Methods</h2>
    <p>Hitori Jigyo Lab promotes partner products through editorial articles, comparison pages, tool hubs, application logs, and context-specific links. We do not position the site as a coupon directory, cashback community, trademark-bidding operation, or mass social posting account.</p>
    <p>Affiliate links are disclosed clearly. We prefer practical, trust-first content that explains who a tool is for, who should avoid it, what to check before payment, and what alternatives may exist.</p>

    <div class="review-score-grid">
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">Content</p>
        <h2>Review Articles</h2>
        <p>Long-form Japanese reviews and setup notes written for small operators.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">Discovery</p>
        <h2>Tool Hubs</h2>
        <p>Use-case based pages for website tools, newsletters, CRM, ecommerce, and analytics.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">Trust</p>
        <h2>Disclosure</h2>
        <p>Affiliate relationships are disclosed and separated from editorial judgment.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="panel-label">Logs</p>
        <h2>Application Records</h2>
        <p>Partner applications, rejections, and improvements are documented as public learning logs.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h2>Current Focus Areas</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Overseas SaaS tools for Japanese solo founders</li>
      <li>AI-assisted workflows and site building</li>
      <li>Newsletter and audience-building tools</li>
      <li>CRM and customer-management tools for small operators</li>
      <li>Image production workflows for affiliate articles</li>
      <li>Analytics and Search Console preparation</li>
      <li>Affiliate network application readiness</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
    <p>We check official pricing pages, help documents, terms, program notes, and real setup experience whenever possible. If a product has not been fully tested yet, we separate research notes from hands-on experience. Pricing and terms can change, so readers are always encouraged to confirm final details on official pages.</p>
    <p>Related Japanese policy pages are available here: <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>, <a href="/review-policy/">Review Criteria</a>, and <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>.</p>

    <h2>Operator</h2>
    <p>TATSU operates Hitori Jigyo Lab as Founder / Publisher. He is based in Fukuoka, Japan, and has long-term experience as a self-employed operator. The site reflects a practical, implementation-focused viewpoint rather than a purely theoretical software review approach.</p>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <p class="panel-label">Contact</p>
      <h2>Partner Inquiries</h2>
      <p>For affiliate program reviews, partnership inquiries, or media information, please contact us through the contact page.</p>
      <p>
        <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact</a>
        <a class="button" href="/affiliate-programs/">Program Status</a>
        <a class="button" href="/compare/">Comparison Pages</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
